    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d339">

                <pb facs="0482" n="470" sameAs="frus:frus1940v03/pg470"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 European War 1939/4094: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Egypt</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Hare</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the
                            Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Cairo</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1940-06-22T18:00:00+02:00">June 22, 1940—6
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received June 23—5:58 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>117. My telegram No. 115, June 22, 8 a.m.<anchor n="8" xml:id="d339-f1"/> An
                    official communiqué issued this afternoon states this morning’s air raid warning
                    in Cairo was a false alarm and that the planes fired upon were Royal Air Force
                    units. Several civilian casualties from anti-aircraft fire reported.</p>
                <pb facs="0483" n="471" xml:id="pg471"/>
                <p>Another communiqué states that 2 persons were killed and 23 wounded during last
                    night’s bombing in Alexandria. Consul there reports no American casualties.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hare</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
